---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Hero from '../../components/Hero.astro';
import Cta from '../../components/Cta.astro';
import SectionNav from '../../components/SectionNav.astro';
---
<Base title={"What to Send When Selling a Hotel Loan"} description={"A one-page summary starts the conversation. The information that lets us give an indication, what diligence needs, and a checklist of a complete hotel loan file."}>
  <Hero eyebrow={"For banks"} title={"What to send, and when."} lead={"A one-page summary starts the conversation. A complete file shortens the time to closing."} />
  <SectionNav section="banks" />
  <main id="main">
<section class="section"><div class="wrap">
      <div class="head"><p class="eyebrow">Two stages</p><h2>Send a little first, and the rest once we are talking.</h2></div>
      <div class="cells two">
        <div><h3>For an indication</h3><ul><li>Unpaid principal balance (<a href="/glossary/#upb">UPB</a>) and accrued interest</li><li>Payment status and maturity date</li><li>Hotel name, brand, location, and room count</li><li>Most recent appraisal, if any</li><li>Whether the hotel is open, and who is operating it</li></ul></div>
        <div><h3>For diligence</h3><ul><li>Note, mortgage, assignments, and guaranties</li><li>Franchise agreement, comfort letter, and improvement plan</li><li>Operating statements and performance reports</li><li>Tax, insurance, and license status</li><li>Default correspondence and any court filings</li></ul></div>
      </div>
    </div></section>

    <section class="section alt"><div class="wrap">
      <div class="head"><p class="eyebrow">A complete file</p><h2>What a buyer expects to find.</h2>
        <p>Buyers discount what they cannot verify. A complete file improves pricing and shortens the time to closing.</p></div>
      <div class="cells">
        <div><h3>Loan</h3><ul><li>Note, endorsements, mortgage, and assignments</li><li>Guaranties, modifications, and forbearance agreements</li><li>Payment history and outstanding advances</li><li>Title policy and security filings on personal property</li></ul></div>
        <div><h3>Franchise and management</h3><ul><li>Franchise agreement and comfort letter</li><li>Default and termination notices from the brand</li><li>Improvement plan and latest quality inspection</li><li>Management agreement</li></ul></div>
        <div><h3>Operations</h3><ul><li>Three years of operating statements, plus year to date</li><li>Monthly performance reports against the competitive set (<a href="/glossary/#str-report">STR reports</a>)</li><li>Occupancy and sales tax filings</li><li>Liquor license and operating permits</li><li>Group bookings and advance deposits</li></ul></div>
        <div><h3>Property and proceedings</h3><ul><li>Latest appraisal, condition report, and environmental report</li><li>Ground lease, if any</li><li>Receiver's order and reports</li><li>Pending litigation and bankruptcy filings</li></ul></div>
      </div>
    </div></section>

    <section class="section"><div class="wrap intro">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Putting a file together</p><h2>Send what you have, and say what is missing.</h2></div>
      <dl class="pillars">
        <div><dt>Start with the summary</dt><dd>You do not need a complete file to get an indicative price.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Name the gaps</dt><dd>A document that cannot be found is easier to price than one that is not mentioned.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>For a pool, start with a loan tape</dt><dd>A <a href="/glossary/#loan-tape">loan tape</a> is one line of key data per loan: balance, status, maturity, collateral, and location. It is the usual first document for a small pool.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Date everything</dt><dd>Operating statements, appraisals, and inspections are only useful if the buyer knows how current they are.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Mind the customer's information</dt><dd>A loan sale involves information the bank is obliged to protect. We sign a confidentiality agreement first, and <a class="more arrow" href="/banks/confidentiality/">here is how we handle it</a>.</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div></section>

    <section class="section alt"><div class="wrap"><div class="head"><p class="eyebrow">Related reading</p></div><ul class="toc"><li><a href="/library/checklist/">Hotel loan diligence checklist <span>Library</span></a></li><li><a href="/blog/reading-a-hotels-operating-statement/">Reading a hotel's operating statement before you price its loan <span>Blog</span></a></li><li><a href="/glossary/#t12">Trailing twelve months (T-12) <span>Glossary</span></a></li><li><a href="/glossary/#comfort-letter">Comfort letter <span>Glossary</span></a></li></ul></div></section>
  </main>
  <Cta title={"Discuss a hotel loan in confidence."} text={"A conversation and an indicative price carry no obligation to sell."} label={"Start a conversation"} />
</Base>
